          "title": "Acquire complete Kordloo2025 waste-aluminum-electrolyte bioleaching evidence",
          "state": "open",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CMMMech/issues/202",
          "body": "The round64 lithium investigation verified the identity of Kordloo et al. (2025), *Lithium recovery from waste aluminum electrolyte via bioleaching: Comparative insights into acidic and alkaline pathways using Aspergillus niger and Glutamicibacter nicotianae*, DOI [10.1016/j.wasman.2025.115043](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.wasman.2025.115043), PMID 40749529. This aluminum-production stream is a potential distinct secondary-resource owner, subject to full feed-provenance review.\n\nThe publisher preview and NCBI abstract do not establish complete methods or controls. The public publisher API returned core metadata only despite a full-text response wrapper; OpenAlex reported no accessible full text. No record, mechanism or CREATE history was admitted from abstract results. The source handoff is staged at `research/sources/round64-lithium/20261014T062345Z-source-investigation.{md,json}`; a permanent link will follow publication.\n\nAcceptance work:\n\n- Acquire the complete original article and relevant supplements through a legitimate accessible route; retain source URL, version, acquisition date and hashes.\n- Verify the process generating the electrolyte waste and distinguish it from spent potlining, anodes, natural ores and battery black mass. Repeat hidden/ignored-inclusive material and study deduplication.\n- Check strain/biomass identity, feed characterization, pretreatment, medium, loadings, pH, duration, replication, sterile and chemistry-matched controls, analytical fractions and denominator calculations.\n- Inspect original plots, phase data and kinetic-fit limits. Preserve null results, contradictions and alternative chemical explanations; do not infer a molecular cause from a fitted kinetic model or isolated-product recovery from dissolved lithium.\n- Curate only supported claims in the appropriate maintained owner, with canonical history, an independent exact-state scientific review and required validation. Otherwise retain an evidence-backed deferral.\n\nThis is a source-acquisition follow-up, not a defect in an accepted record. The documented deferral does not close the evidence gap. No author contact or paid access is requested.\n"
        }
      ]
